<title>SWEDEN: AGA says Q1 profit falls 21 pct.</title>
<headline>AGA says Q1 profit falls 21 pct.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-04-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish medical and industrial gas group AGA on Tuesday reported these earnings for the three months ending March 31, 1997.</p>
<p>					(million crowns unless stated)</p>
<p>Profit after fin items, before</p>
<p> restructuring costs			 414 vs   525</p>
<p> Restructuring costs			 105 vs   nil</p>
<p>Profit after fin items after</p>
<p> restructuring costs			 309 vs   525</p>
<p> Sales					 3,395 vs 3,218</p>
<p>Earnings per share excluding</p>
<p> 1996 capital gain (crowns)	     0.81 vs  1.52</p>
<p> Cost of sales			     2,053 vs  1,902</p>
<p> Selling, development, admin costs     962 vs    885</p>
<p> Associated interest			   7 vs	8</p>
<p> Other operating earnings, net	    45 vs     26</p>
<p> Operating profit			    327 vs    465</p>
<p> Net financial items		 CHARGE 18 vs     60 CREDIT</p>
<p>Capital gain from sale of shares  in Gullspang Kraft			  nil vs  1,794</p>
<p> Pre-tax profit				309 vs  2,319</p>
<p> Taxes					   111 vs    350</p>
<p> Minorities					1 vs	2</p>
<p> Net income				    197 vs  1,967</p>
<p>NOTE -- AGA AB was expected to post a profit of 367 million crowns after financial items for the first quarter, analysts polled by Reuters said. The company had already said the profit would reflect costs of around 100 million crowns because of staff cuts.</p>
<p>-- Stockholm newsroom +46-8-7001017</p>
</text>
